{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/60453-recruitment-post-apocalyptic-blood-and-smoke-pbp","id":60453,"title":"[Recruitment] Post-Apocalyptic Blood and Smoke PbP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-28T21:48:14-08:00","id":60453,"title":"[Recruitment] Post-Apocalyptic Blood and Smoke PbP","content":"No one believed that they would keep the government shut down forever. Reasonable men would surely prevail, and everything would be running smoothly again in days, weeks at most. Everyone was wrong. That many people out of work hurts... not to mention the ripples as necessary government services shut down, one after the other. Sure, regulators only prevented business from happening, but planes can't move without people to direct them, and it's alarming how much of the private sector is actually supported by the government...<br /> <br /> It's been a few years since the end of the resulting economic collapse. The government itself felt the repercussions, as some madmen took it upon themselves to wreak vengeance upon certain members of the administration and Congress. Since then, the United States of America has been nothing but a pipe dream; most communities look out for themselves, with a few resourceful groups running city-states. <br /> <br /> The Masquerade suffered in the chaos. It was difficult for those interested in remaining hidden to do so, especially with so many taking advantage of the sudden lack of unified oversight to do whatever they wished, from feeding to murder. No few vampires lost themselves to the Beast in their unchecked lust for violence, and no few others lost themselves to Final Death as they revealed themselves for what they were. Havens burned and the sunlight reduced neonate and elder alike to ash. Wise elders found the safest places they could and sank into torpor, betting on a more stable future. Now, neonates and ancillae run the All Night Society, with the rare Elder, most of them true monsters, showing his face from time to time. The kine live in smaller communities, sheltering around arable land, living locally, and the enterprising Kindred can make quite a place for himself in these insular groups. Rumors have it that some have set up communes in the places between these city-states, run by loyal ghouls, where they rule as kings; but it's still a safer bet closer to the herd.<br /> <br /> You were Embraced, or rose as a revenant, either during this chaos or shortly after, in a city now known as New Philly. Established in the ruins of what was once Philadelphia, this small city-state has grown to around 100,000 humans, hosting a base of 100 vampires claiming citizenship and an unknown number of unregistered vagrants and nomads. The kine run their side as a localized democratic republic; it's divided into districts, with each district having one vote overall, and each citizen having one vote in his district. The Kindred answer to one Gangrel, whose fierce dominant attitude has driven the local Invictus through this collapse to reclaim the city from the failing Carthians. He enforces a strict, gang-style, turf-based code on the vampires in the city, demanding that each district's Regent enforce his laws throughout the attendant domain. Those who fail are answerable to him and his crew. The Carthians still have a presence in the city, with a small grouping of the least desirable districts to be responsible for. With the increase in insecurities following a major government collapse, religion has experienced a resurgence as well; the Prince has not sided officially with either the Circle or the Lancea et Sanctum, however, and both groups vie for either acceptance or the opportunity to grasp power for themselves. The Ordo Dracul has shrunk in the meantime, with the smallest known number of members. <br /> <br /> This is a game for 3-6 players based in New Philly. I'll be running it using Blood and Smoke rules as written, and the Blood Sorcery book. I'll take the first 6 to send me private messages, and I'll send each of you a questionnaire designed to help build the coterie and fulfill some of the Networking role in the new God-Machine guidelines. Further details are to be determined. I want to be ready to start in as soon as two weeks. Posting procedure will be discussed with players during this time period, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1768-demdemeh","name":"Demdemeh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}